{
  "about": "A chat's photos alone, as the photo opened large pages through them (spec/chat.md, Photos; spec/sync-protocol.md, Chat). seen: whether a reader sees a line's photo among the chat's: `photo` (it is one), `unsent` (taken back), `hidden` (sent in a one-to-one chat while the reader had blocked its writer), `ownChat` (the place's own chat, thread \"group\", not a one-to-one one) and `writerBlocked` (the reader has blocked its writer, whose lines fold away in the place's own chat). page: the chat's photos the reader sees by their lines' `seqs` in order, and a ChatPhotosRequest for those before `seq` (or after it, with `after`; 0 for the latest, or after from the first), `size` a page; `expected` is the page's seqs, how many photos come before it (`offset`) and how many the chat holds (`total`). run: the photos a device holds open large, as steps: `open` with the `held` photos among the lines laid out and the `tapped` one; `page`, a ChatPhotos answering one of its asks (dropped unless `seq` is still the end it asked from); `show`, swiped to a photo; `line`, a new line with a photo the reader sees; `gone`, a line taken back or hidden, `wasPhoto` whether the device knew it as one of the photos (null when it did not hold the line); `lines`, the chat's lines on the device now, each with whether it is a photo the reader sees, the first time only noted, then a new photo past them all added and a photo no longer seen gone; `reconnected`, the socket open again, the asks not yet answered asked again. After each step `expected` is the photos held (`seqs`), how many come before them (`offset`) and in all (`total`), null while unknown, the one shown (null once none is left, which closes it) and the pages newly asked for (`asks`), as `ahead` (chatRules.photoPageAhead) has it: an end's next page once the photo shown is fewer than `ahead` from it, and both ends while `offset` is unknown.",
